<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RELEGATION ROUND RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RELEGATION ROUND RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPERE, Finland 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of relegation</p>
<p>round matches at the ice hockey world championships on</p>
<p>Wednesday:</p>
<p>Norway 3 France 4 (0-1 3-1 0-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Norway - Oystein Olsen (25:15), Rune Fjeldstad (33:25), Atle</p>
<p>Olsen (36:51).</p>
<p>France - Stephane Barin (13:39), Roger Dube (31:49, 43:42),</p>
<p>Philippe Bozon (51:54).</p>
<p>Penaltis: Norway 12 minutes, France 12.</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,276.</p>
<p>Italy 5 Germany 2 (0-1 3-1 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Italy - Dino Felcetti (21:45), Robert Nardella (31:26),</p>
<p>Bruno Zarrillo (33:03, 59:49), Gaetano Orlando (47:58).</p>
<p>Germany - Reemt Pyka (15:24), Jochen Hecht (29:04).</p>
<p>Penalties: Italy 14 minutes, Germany 10</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,403</p>
<p>    Standings	  P   W  D  L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> 1. Italy		3   2  1  0  12   8    5</p>
<p> 2. Latvia	     3   2  0  1  18   8    4</p>
<p> 3. Slovakia	   3   2  0  1   7   5    4</p>
<p> 4. France	     3   2  0  1   9   9    4</p>
<p> 5. Germany	    4   1  0  3   4  15    2</p>
<p> 6. Norway	     4   0  1  3   9  14    1</p>
<p>Next matches: Italy v Slovakia, Latvia v France (Thursday)</p>
